  "title": "Gawhar Shad",
  "summary": "Gawhar Shad was the wife and consort of the Timurid ruler Shahrukh and, after his death in 1447, acted as de facto ruler for about a decade while arranging the coronation of her young grandson. She paid for two Friday mosques, in Herat and Mashhad, and was patron of a madrasa in Herat completed in 1432/3. One source gives her life as 1378–1457.",
